  "prompt_prefix": "/deep-research ",
  "instruction": "According to fishbase.org, what is the FishBase Name and species of every fish in Japan that has a highly commercial designation in both the \"use\" column and the \"use elsewhere\" column?",
  "answer": "Based on FishBase's commercial species list for Japan (`c_code=392`), **12 fish species** have \"highly commercial\" designation in both the \"Use\" (in Japan) and \"Use elsewhere\" (global) columns.\n\n| FishBase Name | Species (Scientific Name) |\n|---------------|---------------------------|\n| Alaska pollock | *Gadus chalcogrammus* |\n| Ayu sweetfish | *Plecoglossus altivelis* |\n| Deepwater longtail red snapper | *Etelis coruscans* |\n| Engraulis japonicus | Japanese anchovy |\n| Japanese amberjack | *Seriola quinqueradiata* |\n| Japanese pufferfish | *Takifugu rubripes* |\n| Japanese scad | *Decapterus maruadsi* |\n| Pacific Chub mackerel | *Scomber japonicus* |\n| Pacific cod | *Gadus macrocephalus* |\n| Pacific sandlance | *Ammodytes personatus* |\n| Red seabream | *Pagrus major* |\n| Yellowfin tuna | *Thunnus albacares* |\n\n**Source:** FishBase Country Commercial Species List for Japan — `https://www.fishbase.se/country/CountrySearchList.php?c_code=392&group=commercial` [1]\n\n**Notes:**\n- Data extracted from the `table_data_arr` JavaScript variable in the page, which contains the full commercial species table with \"Use\" and \"Use elsewhere\" columns.\n- \"Use\" = importance in Japan's fisheries (from FishBase COUNTRIES table \"Importance\" field)\n- \"Use elsewhere\" = global/general importance (from FishBase SPECIES table \"Fisheries\" field, plus \"bycatch\" category)\n- Both fields use the same classification: `highly commercial`, `commercial`, `minor commercial`, `subsistence fisheries`, `of potential interest`, `of no interest` (with \"bycatch\" added for \"Use elsewhere\") [2] [3]\n\n[1] https://www.fishbase.se/country/CountrySearchList.php?c_code=392&group=commercial\n[2] https://www.fishbase.se/manual/fishbasethe_countries_table.htm\n[3] https://www.fishbase.se/manual/fishbasethe_species_table.htm",
  "answer_chars": 1799,
  "expected_answer": "Pacific sandlance (Ammodytes personatus), Japanese Scad (Decapterus maruadsi), Japanese anchovy (Engraulis japonicus), Deepwater longtail red snapper (Etelis coruscans), Alaska pollack (Gadus chalcogrammus), Pacific cod (Gadus macrocephalus), Red seabream (Pagrus major), Ayu sweetfish (Plecoglossus altivelis), Chub mackerel (Scomber japonicus), Japanese amberjack (Seriola quinqueradiata), Japanese pufferfish (Takifugu rubripes), Yellowfin tuna (Thunnus albacares)",
